  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In an October 7, 2026 official statement, Roger D. Klein said reliable clinical evidence is critical and that new technologies could enable faster, more consistent, and more reproducible evidence synthesis. In a September 24, 2025 newsletter, he said the agency is prioritizing next-generation tools such as artificial intelligence and alternative testing models while continuing to rely on real-world data. In an undated reported LinkedIn statement, he said the Trump administration is committed to American leadership in super intelligence and to ensuring its benefits reach the American people.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3"
   ],
   "sentences": [
